  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you cast a spell that targets only one creature and doesn't have a range of self, you can spend a number of sorcery points equal to the spell's level to target a second creature in range with the same spell (1 sorcery point if the spell is a cantrip).</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Foundry Note: Once adding this to a sheet, you will need to tell it what resource to consume when used.</p>\n<p>When casting Twinned Spell with a spell level higher than one, you will have to manually input the number of Sorcery Points consumed.</p>",
